GitHub's web-flow commit signing key, pinned for vdeploy (GH-221).

  9684 79A1 AFF9 27E3 7D1A  566B B569 0EEE BB95 2194
  rsa4096, created 2024-01-16, "GitHub <noreply@github.com>"

GitHub signs every merge made through its web UI or API (a PR's squash merge) with
this key. Fetched from https://github.com/web-flow.gpg on 2026-11-22. That file also
holds the 2017 key 5DE3 E050 9C47 EA3C F04A  42D3 4AEE 18F8 3AFD EB23, which expired
on 2024-01-16 and signs no commit on main since the ruleset of 2026-11-20 (see #221's
measurement), so it is not pinned here.

features/nix/vdeploy builds a keyring from this file at Nix build time
(trustedSigningKeys), and vdeploy deploys a head of main only when its signature
verifies against that keyring (requireSignedCommits). When GitHub rotates the key,
add the new one here, and keep this one while main still needs it.

